<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Brega</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 1100 CE (approx.) · capital Knowth</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A kingdom of the southern Ui Neill on the fertile plain north of Dublin, home to Tara, Knowth and Newgrange and rival of Mide.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Brega emerged in the 7th century when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sil-naedo-slaine">Sil nAedo Slaine</a>, descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aed-slaine">Aed Slaine</a> of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Ui Neill</a>, established themselves in the plain of Brega, stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-liffey">Liffey</a> northwards across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-boyne">Boyne</a>. Their rulers made the ancient passage tomb at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knowth">Knowth</a> into a royal residence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Brega's kings shared the kingship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-of-tara">Tara</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mide">Clann Cholmain</a> and the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Ui Neill</a>, holding it often in the 7th and early 8th centuries and once more under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congalach-cnogba">Congalach Cnogba</a> in the 10th. The kingdom split into northern and southern parts. It contained monasteries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slane">Slane</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duleek">Duleek</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monasterboice">Monasterboice</a>, and from the 9th century suffered heavy pressure from the Norse of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dublin">Kingdom of Dublin</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the 11th century Brega was fragmented and dominated by Mide, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a>. Its lands passed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-meath">Lordship of Meath</a> granted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-de-lacy-lord-of-meath">Hugh de Lacy</a> in 1172, and its name survives in Irish place-names.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 600 CE – 1100 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.64%;width:9.95%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 1100 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Knowth</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aed Slaine, Congalach Cnogba</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Brega, Sil nAedo Slaine</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=850&amp;focus=kingdom-of-brega" aria-label="Kingdom of Brega on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4536 333 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Brega lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4856 589L4853 592"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4853 592h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4856 589h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4856 589h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Knowth. <a href="/atlas?year=850&amp;focus=kingdom-of-brega">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
